{"milestone": "M7_memory_report", "step": 24, "tool": "command_execution", "tool_output": "# Memory-Aware Retrospective\n\n## Sources\n\n- `memory/memory_summary.md`\n- `docs/compatibility-notes.md`\n- `benchmarks/perf-baseline.json`\n- `tmp/report.json`\n- `tmp/acceptance-report.json`\n- `tmp/hidden-acceptance-report.json`\n- `tmp/acceptance-subdir-report.json`\n\n## Design Decisions\n\nThe earlier design record in `memory/memory_summary.md` says the CLI keeps the `run`\nsubcommand, configuration files stay optional, all internal paths resolve from the\nrepo root, and the report stage reads only cleaned records plus rejects. The same\nmemory note also records the historical testing preference: cover retry behavior\nand rejects first, then expand report fields.\n\n## Current Artifacts\n\nThe current report artifacts agree on the final sample result:\n\n- `processed_count`: 4\n- `rejected_count`: 2\n- `retry_count`: 0\n- `source_files`: `data/input.csv`, `data/events.jsonl`\n- DAG stages logged: `extract`, `clean`, `report`\n- DAG status: all stages succeeded on attempt 1\n- memory citation in report output: `memory/memory_summary.md`\n\nThe rejected records are real cleaning outcomes: one CSV row has an empty `id`,\nand one JSONL event lacks `id`.\n\n## Compatibility And Performance Notes\n\n`docs/compatibility-notes.md` says the current compatibility record is limited to\nthis fixture environment and is not a formal Python version matrix. The workbench\nshim keeps `python -m mini_harness` usable from `subdir/workbench`, but this is\nverified only for the current fixture layout.\n\n`benchmarks/perf-baseline.json` describes a tiny local fixture sample with 5 input\nrows, so it is useful as a smoke baseline, not as a general performance benchmark.\n\n## Final Summary\n\nThe implementation matches the remembered design direction: a stable `run`\nsubcommand, optional JSON/YAML configuration, repo-root-relative path handling,\nand a report based on actual cleaned and rejected records. Current artifacts show\n4 processed records, 2 rejected records, no retries in the acceptance reports, and\nsuccessful extract/clean/report execution.\n\r\n", "tool_error": false, "event_type": "tool_result", "event_id": "item_11"}
